* Fender '65 Deluxe Reverb reissue (drawing 041285 rev B) preamp: Normal channel (V1A, tone stack, V1B) and
* Vibrato channel (V2A, tone stack, V2B), the V4B mixer stage that follows the Vibrato channel, and the
* Normal/Vibrato mixing network that feeds the phase inverter. Transcribed from the schematic; it is the
* Twin Reverb's preamp with the Deluxe's differences:
*  - the tone stacks have no Middle control: a fixed 6.8k (R9, R21) sits where the Twin's 10k pot is;
*  - the preamp rail is 261 V (TP4) instead of 393 V;
*  - V4B's plate and V4A's plate loads are 100k, the reverb pot feeds the mixer through R32 470k alone.
*
* Not modelled: the Bright switches and the reverb footswitch. The vibrato oscillator is in vibrato.net; only
* its photocell is here (R_CELL). Where the drawing is hard to follow (how the Intensity pot reaches the mixing
* node) this keeps the Twin's arrangement.
*
* Reading notes (same as the Twin):
*  - jacks: Input 1 puts the signal on N1 (1M to ground) and, because the unused Input 2 switch ties T1 to N1,
*    reaches the grid through 68k || 68k; Input 2 feeds T1 with the unused Input 1 switch grounding N1, so the
*    68k + 68k pair divides by two (-6 dB). Both unplugged jacks of the idle channel ground its grid.
*  - tone stacks: C 250p from the plate to the treble pot, 100k slope resistor to the bass capacitors (0.1u,
*    0.047u), bass 250k as a rheostat in the ground leg, 6.8k to ground, treble wiper = output into the
*    volume pot (1M). Tapers 30A / 10A.
*  - V1B and V2B share the 820/22u cathode network; V4A and V4B share 820/22u too.
*  - the cut for the power amp is after the mixing network at node m1.

* 261 V rail (node x, TP4), driven from the power amp at run time.
V VRAIL x 100 261
* The guitar behind a variable source resistance, then the four jacks.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance. RSRC is the plain 7k source: the "Off" setting, and what a pedal in front of the amp
* looks like. A pickup replaces it with its own impedance as seen from the open-circuit voltage (the recording): the
* coil (winding resistance RPU + inductance) in parallel with its winding capacitance CPU and an eddy-current loss resistor
* RPL, then the cable capacitance (200 pF per 2 m, switched in steps of 200, 400 and 800 pF). The engine sets the values:
* single coil = coil 1 (2.5 H), humbucker and P-90 = coil 2 (5 H) with their own resistances; open = 1e12.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

* Normal channel jacks: SW_N1/SW_N2 route the signal to N1 / T1; SW_NTN (T1 tied to N1) and SW_NNG
* (N1 grounded) are the unplugged-jack switches. Closed 1 ohm / open 1e12, set by the jack modes.
R SW_N1 in nn 1e12
R SW_N2 in nt 1e12
R SW_NTN nt nn 1
R SW_NNG nn 0 1
R R3 nn 0 1M
R R1 nt ng 68k
R R2 ng nn 68k

* Vibrato channel jacks (J3 = Input 1, J4 = Input 2).
R SW_V1 in vn 1
R SW_V2 in vt 1e12
R SW_VTN vt vn 1
R SW_VNG vn 0 1e12
R R14 vn 0 1M
R R12 vt vg 68k
R R13 vg vn 68k

* Normal channel: V1A with its tone stack and V1B.
T V1A ng pa1 ka1 12AX7
R R4 x pa1 100k
R R5 ka1 0 1k5
C C1 ka1 0 22u
C C2 pa1 nt1 250p
R R6 pa1 nb1 100k
C C3 nb1 nu1 0.1u
C C4 nb1 nm1 0.047u
R VR_TT_N nt1 no1 1
R VR_TB_N no1 nu1 1
R VR_BASS_N nu1 nm1 1
R R9 nm1 0 6k8
R VR_VT_N no1 gb1 1
R VR_VB_N gb1 0 1
T V1B gb1 pb1 kb 12AX7
R R11 x pb1 100k

* Vibrato channel: V2A with its tone stack and V2B.
T V2A vg pa2 ka2 12AX7
R R16 x pa2 100k
R R17 ka2 0 1k5
C C6 ka2 0 22u
C C7 pa2 nt2 250p
R R18 pa2 nb2 100k
C C8 nb2 nu2 0.1u
C C9 nb2 nm2 0.047u
R VR_TT_V nt2 no2 1
R VR_TB_V no2 nu2 1
R VR_BASS_V nu2 nm2 1
R R21 nm2 0 6k8
R VR_VT_V no2 gb2 1
R VR_VB_V gb2 0 1
T V2B gb2 pb2 kb 12AX7
R R29 x pb2 100k
* Cathode of V1B and V2B.
R R24 kb 0 820
C C11 kb 0 22u

* Vibrato channel into V4B: 0.022u, then 3.3M (10p across it) against 220k and the reverb return (470k from the
* Reverb pot's wiper).
C C12 pb2 qa 22n
R R25 qa q 3M3
C C13 qa q 10p
R R33 q 0 220k
R R32 rw q 470k
T V4B q p4 k4 12AX7
R R34 x p4 100k
R R30 k4 0 820
C C16 k4 0 22u

* Reverb, the part that loads and joins this circuit (the tubes and the transformer are in reverb.net): the 500p
* / 1M tap that feeds V3's grid, and V4A's plate signal, behind its ~38k output impedance (100k plate load in
* parallel with the tube), through 3.3n into the 100k Reverb pot. V4A's idle current in the cathode shared with
* V4B is a resistor to the rail (about 0.85 mA at 261 V).
C C14 qa gv3 500p
R R26 gv3 0 1M
S VREVOUT pv4m 38k 0
C C17 pv4m rt 3n3
R VR_REV_T rt rw 1
R VR_REV_B rw 0 1
R RV4A x k4 300k
* Mixer: V4B plate through 0.1u into m2; the Normal channel through 0.047u + 220k into m1; 220k between.
C C18 p4 m2 0.1u
C C5 pb1 a1 0.047u
R R12M a1 m1 220k
R R35 m2 m1 220k
* DC reference for the floating mixing nodes (the real one is the phase inverter's grid network).
R RDC m1 0 100M
* Intensity pot (50k, wiper to the OP1 photocell, which the vibrato circuit sets) shunting the mixing node m2.
* With the vibrato off the cell is dark and the 50k remains as a load.
R VR_INT_T m2 wi 1
R VR_INT_B wi 0 1
R R_CELL wi 0 2M
* Load of the phase inverter input: 1n coupling cap and the 1M grid network.
C C25L m1 pl 1n
R RPI pl 0 1M
